\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Praise, for Thee in Zion waits;
\par Prayer shall besiege Thy temple gates;
\par All flesh shall to Thy throne repair,
\par And find, through Christ, salvation 
\par there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our spirits faint, our sins prevail;
\par Leave not our trembling hearts to fail:
\par O Thou that hearest prayer, descend,
\par And still be found the sinner's friend.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. How blest THy saints; how safely led;
\par How surely kept; how richly fed!
\par Saviour of all in earth and sea,
\par How happy they who rest in Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thy hand sets fast the mighty hills,
\par Thy voice the troubled ocean stills;
\par Evening and morning hymn Thy praise,
\par And earth Thy bounty wide displays.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The year is with Thy goodness crowned,
\par Thy clouds drop wealth the world around;
\par Through Thee the deserts laugh and sing,
\par And nature smiles, and owns her King.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Lord, on our souls Thy Spirit pour;
\par The moral waste within restore;
\par O let Thy love our spring- tide be,
\par And make us all bear fruit to Thee.
\par                             Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

